  "how does he know the retrieval is actually working?": {
    "answer": "He knows retrieval is actually working when a retrieved chunk earns its place in the context window and the top-k is a ceiling rather than a quota. He also knows it when a query like \"Growaza\" or \"NCP-AAI\" lands one chunk far clear of everything else, causing the keyword hit to be decisive and skipping the embedding call. He knows it when the retrieval produces exact ties that are broken by the better single rank, and when the projection drawn beside the page uses classical multidimensional scaling on the full cosine distance matrix rather than UMAP or t-SNE.",
